{"type": "assistant", "timestamp": "2026-10-15T11:46:07.817Z", "message": {"role": "assistant", "model": "claude-opus-5-5", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "I fixed `aggregate()` in `aggregate.py`. `python3 -m unittest discover` passes all 8 tests: the 2 in `test_visible.py` and 6 new ones in `test_aggregate.py`.\n\nWhat I changed:\n\n- **Parsing.** I use `csv.reader(strict=True)` instead of `DictReader`, because `DictReader` silently accepts short rows, extra columns and duplicate headers. CSV parse errors (`csv.Error`) now raise `ValueError`.\n- **Header.** The first non-blank row is the header. It must have exactly 4 cells that are the set `{id,currency,kind,amount}`, in any order and without duplicates. If there is no header, or only a header, the result is `{}`.\n- **Row checks.** Each row must have exactly 4 columns, and spaces are stripped from every value. `id` must not be empty, `currency` must be exactly `RUB`, `USD` or `EUR`, and `kind` must be `payment` or `refund`. The amount must fully match `[0-9]+(?:\\.[0-9]+)?`, so signs, exponents, NaN, Infinity, `.5`, `5.` and non-ASCII digits are all rejected.\n- **Sums.** Each row is rounded to 0.01 with `ROUND_HALF_UP` before it is added or subtracted, so `0.125 + 0.125` gives `0.26`, not `0.25`. Totals start at `Decimal('0.00')`, so zero totals stay in the result. Values are always `Decimal`.\n- **Large amounts.** I raised the Decimal precision to `MAX_PREC` for this function. With the default precision (28 digits), long amounts raise `InvalidOperation`, which is not a `ValueError`.\n- **Repeated IDs.** A repeat with the same currency, kind and rounded amount is counted once. Any other repeat raises `ValueError`.\n\nTwo choices the task left open:\n- I also strip spaces from header names, so ` amount , kind,...` is accepted.\n- A blank line or a line of only spaces is skipped, but `,,,` raises `ValueError` because it is a 4-column row with an empty `id`.\n\nThe test run left a `__pycache__/` folder. I tried to delete it, but the shell rejected `rm -rf`, so it is still there. It is harmless."}], "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 181, "cache_read_input_tokens": 203659, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 181}, "output_tokens": 5}}, "is_main_assistant": true, "source_line": 152}
